OL,3,AUK falls silent to mark Armistice Day
OL,4,
OL,5,FThe UK has fallen silent to mark
OL,6,FArmistice Day, commemorating the end of
OL,7,FWorld War One.
OL,9,FThe two-minute silence took place to
OL,10,Fmark the end of the war and to remember
OL,11,Fthose who have died in conflicts.
OL,13,FCeremonies took place at the Cenotaph
OL,14,Fin London, the National Memorial
OL,15,FArboretum in Staffordshire, and across
OL,16,Fthe UK.
OL,18,FDefence Secretary Wes Streeting laid a
OL,19,Fwreath at the Cenotaph memorial, which
OL,20,Fwas also attended by senior military
OL,21,Ffigures, schoolchildren and cadets.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
